__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
node_modules/
.next/

# The cold store. Raw archived registry versions, content-addressed.
# Measured at ~1.5 GB gzipped across the frame, so it cannot be committed.
#
# It is NOT "reproducible from the manifest" -- an earlier version of this
# comment said so and was wrong. The manifest records each document's SHA-256,
# which lets a holder VERIFY the bytes; it cannot regenerate them, and if the
# undocumented archive endpoints disappear nothing re-fetches them.
#
# What is committed instead is data/register/: the hashes and the extracted
# fields the analysis consumes. See README, "What is durable, stated precisely".
data/cold/

# Derived analytical artefacts. Everything here is a pure function of the cold
# store plus a pinned pipeline commit, so committing it would be committing a
# cache (SRS 6.3).
data/warehouse/
data/serve/

# data/pilot/ IS committed. It is the evidence for FEASIBILITY.md, and a
# feasibility claim whose measurements are not in the repository is an assertion.
